.TH SATELLITE 1 "2026-11-23" "Satellite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
satellite \- receive game controllers from Dish clients over the network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B satellite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B satellite
is the receiver of the Dish family. Dish for Android, Dish for iOS, Dish for
macOS, Dish for Windows and Dish for Linux pair with it over the local network
and stream their controllers' input to it; Satellite presents each controller
to the games on this machine as a virtual gamepad created through
.IR /dev/uinput .
.PP
It takes no command-line arguments. It runs in the background, with a tray
icon where the desktop has an AppIndicator host and headless otherwise, and is
configured through its dashboard at
.UR http://localhost:9877
.UE ,
which only this machine can reach.
.SH NETWORK
UDP port 9876 carries the encrypted controller stream, TCP port 9443 the
pairing and session API over TLS, and mDNS on UDP 5353 (with a legacy beacon on
UDP 9879) lets clients find the receiver.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SATELLITE_CONFIG_DIR
Where the configuration and the pairing keys are kept, in place of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/satellite .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
The log is written under
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/satellite/logs
(default
.IR ~/.local/state/satellite/logs ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-satellite-uinput.rules
Grants the seat user, and the
.B input
group, access to
.IR /dev/uinput .
.TP
.I /usr/share/satellite/web
The dashboard and the bundled controller database.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT shut Satellite down cleanly, and it exits 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/TinkerNorth/satellite
.UE ,
.UR https://dish.tinkernorth.com
.UE
